  "final_text": "All four steps are done. The rule reads back as enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has the time field `timestamp`. The response code field is `response`, aggregated through `response.keyword`.\n- **Dashboard:** 'S4-bc32be53 Web logs' (`s4-bc32be53-web-logs-4f7014e090da`) has two panels: a line chart of request count over `timestamp`, and a bar chart of request count by `response.keyword`.\n- **Alert rule:** 'S4-bc32be53 5xx errors' (`d66324f0-298a-40d4-9d80-d0c89cbb06af`) runs every 1m. It is a `.es-query` rule that counts documents where `response.keyword` is in the range 500\u2013599 over a 5m window, and fires when the count is greater than 10. It was created disabled and I enabled it. Read-back shows `enabled: true`, status `ok`.\n- **Panel rename:** The response-code panel is now titled 'Responses by code'. Read-back confirms the dashboard shows that title.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The 500\u2013599 filter uses a lexicographic range on the keyword field. That is correct for three-digit codes, but a non-three-digit value in that field would be handled differently.\n- I used a bar chart for the response-code panel. Your spec did not name a chart type.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
